law.text:
		Local public agencies represented on local interagency coordinating councils are responsible for:

Providing services as appropriate and agreed upon by members of the local interagency coordinating council;


Maintaining data and providing information as requested to their respective state agencies;


Developing and implementing interagency agreements;


Complying with applicable state and federal regulations and local policies and procedures; and


Following procedural safeguards and dispute resolution procedures as adopted by the Commonwealth.
